<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n114732" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρο-ΐζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρῴζω</span>
			, <i>touch the surface</i> of a body, and generally,
				<i>touch,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἥβας χροΐζει λέχος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Heracl.</u>
					915
				</span></i>
			(lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				139.6
			</span></i>(
				Med.
			):—
				Med.
			, <i>touch another's skin with one's own, lie with,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>, of a woman, Theocr.<i><span class="en">
				10.18
			</span></i> (in 
				Dor.
			
			fut.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χροϊξεῖται</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>colour, stain,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. ἐπ᾽ ὀλίγον ἀγχούσῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dsc.
					2.80
				</span></i>
			; poet. aor.
			
				Pass.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χροιισθεῖσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					74.26
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				17(2).275
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
